# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build91 Studio — environment variables (committable example)
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored by Next.js; this file (.env.example) is not.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Quote engine — outbound email via Resend ─────────────────────────
# Sign up free at https://resend.com and paste the API key here.
# Without this key, /api/quote still works — it just logs submissions to
# the server console instead of emailing them.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
#   QUOTE_TO_EMAIL  — where quote submissions are delivered.
#                     Default: amitmathur@gmail.com
#   RESEND_FROM     — sender. Use `onboarding@resend.dev` while on the
#                     Resend free tier; switch to `quote@build91.in`
#                     once you verify your domain in Resend.
#                     Default: "Build91 Quote <onboarding@resend.dev>"
QUOTE_TO_EMAIL=contact@build91.in
RESEND_FROM="Build91 Studio <noreply@studio.build91.in>"

# ─── Google Places API — live rating shown below VideoHero ────────────
# Server-side fetch only, 24h ISR cache (see lib/googleRating.ts).
# NEVER expose to the browser — the variable name omits the NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix on purpose so Next.js won't bundle it into client code.
#
# Setup checklist:
#   1. Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Library → enable
#      "Places API (New)" (NOT the legacy "Places API")
#   2. Credentials → Create API key
#   3. Restrict the key:
#       • Application restriction: None (server-side has no Referer)
#       • API restriction: Restrict key → ONLY "Places API (New)"
#   4. IAM & Admin → Quotas → set a daily cap (~500 calls/day)
#   5. Billing → set a $5/month alert as a safety net
#
# Place ID for Build91 Studio Raipur is hardcoded below — replace if you
# ever migrate the Google Business Profile to a different listing.
# Lookup tool: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-id
#
# Without these vars set, GoogleRatingBand silently falls back to its
# hardcoded value (see lib/googleRating.ts → FALLBACK_RATING).
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=AIzaSyXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
GOOGLE_PLACE_ID=ChIJxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Instagram Graph API — "Selected Work" reel grid ──────────────────
# Server-side fetch only, 4h ISR cache (see lib/instagram.ts).
# NEVER expose to the browser — the variable names omit NEXT_PUBLIC_
# on purpose so Next.js won't bundle them into client code.
#
# This integration uses the Instagram API with Instagram Login flavour
# (host: graph.instagram.com, IGAA-prefix tokens — NOT the Facebook
# Page-linked flow). Tokens are long-lived (60 days) and refreshed
# weekly by the Vercel Cron at /api/cron/refresh-instagram-token.
#
# Setup checklist:
#   1. Instagram account → Settings → Account type and tools →
#      switch to Business or Creator (required; personal won't work)
#   2. https://developers.facebook.com → Create App → type Business →
#      add product "Instagram Graph API"
#   3. Graph API Explorer → generate long-lived user access token with
#      `instagram_basic`, `pages_show_list`, `pages_read_engagement`
#   4. Find your IG Business Account ID:
#        GET /me/accounts → grab the Page ID
#        GET /{PAGE_ID}?fields=instagram_business_account → grab the IG ID
#   5. Paste the token below and the IG ID. Verify with:
#        curl "https://graph.instagram.com/${IG_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID}/media?fields=id,media_product_type&access_token=${IG_ACCESS_TOKEN}&limit=3"
#
# Without these vars set (or KV-stored token), SelectedWork silently falls
# back to the 6 reels in lib/instagram-fallback.ts.
IG_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID=00000000000000000
IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=IGAAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Vercel KV — rotating IG token storage ────────────────────────────
# Required for the weekly cron-driven token refresh to persist across
# serverless invocations. Without KV, the cron will refresh the token
# but won't be able to save it — IG_ACCESS_TOKEN above would need to be
# rotated manually every ~50 days.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Vercel dashboard → Storage → Create Database → KV (Redis)
#   2. Connect to this project — Vercel auto-injects these two vars in
#      Preview + Production environments
#   3. For local dev, click "Show secret" on the KV store and paste both
#      values below into .env.local
KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-store.kv.vercel-storage.com
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=AYYYYxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Cron secret — protects /api/cron/refresh-instagram-token ─────────
# Vercel Cron auto-sends Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} when this
# env var is set. Generate any random 32+ char string and paste it.
# Without it set, the cron route runs unauthenticated (fine in dev,
# never in production).
CRON_SECRET=replace-with-random-32-char-string
